    backlog:scopeCompletionState backlog:Proposed ;
    backlog:hasScopeStatementText "IN: chapters 21 (Making Graphs and Manipulating Images), 22 (Recognizing Text in Images), 23 (Controlling the Keyboard and Mouse), 24 (Text-to-Speech and Speech Recognition) and 25 (Threads) of the 3rd edition, in that order. (a) Conversion: examples, result visuals, words and plan of each first-version deck move into a spec for the generic chapter deck builder, so each deck is rebuilt once; the chapter-code manifest is written from it. (b) Deck: titles of at least four words, one thing to look at per slide, plain code without prompts, no lambda unless taught, no text frames overlapping, chapter-code manifest equal to the deck's code in order, no slides added (fuller plain sentences go in speech balloons); the new deck is released in the chapter folder under 03-materials. (c) Reader: notes of 60 to 140 words written to the reader, no directions to a presenter, no think-of statement, each note linking to another slide, chapter or concept; one story balloon and two result balloons on every code slide. (d) No everyday analogies in the decks and pages of chapters 21 to 25; the plain meanings stay. (e) Page: a new page version built from the corrected deck and manifest by the lambda-free page pipeline with a page A-box, passing the full page test. (f) Page code: every page has a top menu item that runs the slide examples in order and conforms to the page shapes; code equal on slide, page and manifest. (g) Release: automatic checks and three recorded review verdicts per chapter before release. (h) Own version: every changed file gets its own version; older page drafts beside the newest page are removed from the tree (kept in git history) and the version check exits 0. (i) Measures: the four measures named open in the mission stage are read before any goal rests on them. FOLDERS THAT MAY CHANGE: 03-materials/ch21 to ch25 (except rdodi/), 08-tooling and 07-lineage. OUT: see the five exclusions." ;
    rdfs:label "Rebuild chapter 21 to 25 decks and pages to the owner's rulings"@en .
